hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16088","He said, Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, he said, al-Muraqqi ibn Sayfi narrated to me, from his grandfather Rabah ibn al-Rabi, brother of Hanzalah the scribe, that he informed him that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a raid he raided, and upon his vanguard was Khalid ibn al-Walid. So Rabah and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a slain woman of what the vanguard had struck, and they stood looking at her and marveling at her creation, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught up with them upon his mount, and they parted from her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon her and said: This one was not to fight. And he said to one of them: Catch up with Khalid, and say to him, do not kill offspring, nor a hireling. He said."
"16089","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, he said, al-Muraqqi ibn Sayfi ibn Rabah informed me, that Rabah, his grandfather, Ibn al-Rabi, informed him that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith."
"16090","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Muraqqi ibn Sayfi ibn Rabah, brother of Hanzalah the scribe, he said, my grandfather informed me that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith. He said."
"16091","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said, I was informed from Abu al-Zinad, he said, Muraqqi ibn Sayfi al-Tamimi informed me, he witnessed upon his grandfather Rabah ibn Rabi al-Hanzali the scribe, that he informed him that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a raid, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Abi al-Zinad."
